{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-65574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ)$ with $R>0$, what is the value of $R?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-65574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+9 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =13 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-65574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6f5976a4f3b7ae0c4367c6ed3ea13ef1dbfee31899a5807a9a6e02ab8b94c63"} {"question" "q-65574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-65574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\sqrt{13}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-65574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{5}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6f5976a4f3b7ae0c4367c6ed3ea13ef1dbfee31899a5807a9a6e02ab8b94c63"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{20}^{∘}"] ["math" "{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "{45}^{∘}"] ["math" "{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "{80}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-80135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6f5976a4f3b7ae0c4367c6ed3ea13ef1dbfee31899a5807a9a6e02ab8b94c63"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{4})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.730\\,\\text{rad}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =9 \\\\ R & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6f5976a4f3b7ae0c4367c6ed3ea13ef1dbfee31899a5807a9a6e02ab8b94c63"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.841)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.841)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.741)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-107574" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+0.730)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,≈\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})≈1.061\\text{ }\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)^{2}+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =5+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =21 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)≈\\sqrt{21}\\,sin\\,(6x-1.061).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6f5976a4f3b7ae0c4367c6ed3ea13ef1dbfee31899a5807a9a6e02ab8b94c63"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{21}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"} {"question" "q-327988" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.061"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13968928/state.json" "file_sha256" "ed8ca2b33289091ef8e5fc5ac4fa76030539521fe4e33fbaa7bf145f76ed5051"}] "usage" {} "basis" 736 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
